    "98d24723-ccea-4ea3-ac19-d0bd11dda36d": {
      "id": "98d24723-ccea-4ea3-ac19-d0bd11dda36d",
      "message": {
        "id": "98d24723-ccea-4ea3-ac19-d0bd11dda36d",
        "author": {
          "role": "assistant",
          "name": null,
          "metadata": {}
        },
        "create_time": 1770909095.093534,
        "update_time": null,
        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "If you’re asking about **devices used to detect illicit drugs**, there are several types used by law enforcement, border services, workplaces, and medical settings.\n\nHere’s a clear breakdown:\n\n---\n\n## 1️⃣ Portable Drug Testing Kits (Field Test Kits)\n- Small chemical kits\n- Substance is placed in a vial → color change indicates possible drug type\n- Used by police for quick roadside or field identification  \n- **Limitation:** Presumptive only (not 100% accurate)\n\n---\n\n## 2️⃣ Drug Testing Devices (Biological Testing)\n\nThese test a person rather than a substance.\n\n### 🔹 Urine Test Kits\n- Most common workplace test\n- Detects drugs like cannabis, cocaine, opioids, amphetamines\n- Detection window: 1–7 days (varies by drug)\n\n### 🔹 Saliva (Oral Fluid) Test\n- Used for roadside drug testing\n- Detects recent use (usually 6–48 hours)\n\n### 🔹 Hair Testing\n- Detects drug use up to 90 days\n- Used in legal or employment cases\n\n### 🔹 Blood Testing\n- Most accurate\n- Used in hospitals or serious legal cases\n\n---\n\n## 3️⃣ Electronic Drug Detection Devices\n\n### 🔹 Ion Mobility Spectrometry (IMS)\n- Detects trace drug particles\n- Used at airports and border crossings\n\n### 🔹 Handheld Spectrometers (Raman / FTIR)\n- Non-contact testing through plastic bags\n- Used by law enforcement\n\n---\n\n## 4️⃣ Drug Detection Sensors / Emerging Tech\n- Portable AI-based analyzers\n- Smartphone-connected test strips\n- Wastewater drug monitoring systems (public health)\n\n---\n\nIf you tell me:\n- Are you asking for **personal testing**,  \n- **Workplace use**,  \n- **Law enforcement equipment**, or  \n- **Technical design information** (engineering side)?  \n\nI can give you more specific guidance.\n\nAlso, since you're in Canada, regulations differ slightly depending on province — let me know if this is for Ontario, BC, etc."
          ]
        },
