    "83a00859-67bd-47ac-9e90-40699b188758": {
      "id": "83a00859-67bd-47ac-9e90-40699b188758",
      "message": {
        "id": "83a00859-67bd-47ac-9e90-40699b188758",
        "author": {
          "role": "assistant",
          "name": null,
          "metadata": {}
        },
        "create_time": 1770909163.198159,
        "update_time": null,
        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "If you mean **detecting illicit drugs hidden behind walls**, there’s no simple consumer device that can just “scan” a wall and show drugs inside.\n\nHere’s how it realistically works:\n\n---\n\n## 🚫 What Does *Not* Exist\n- ❌ No handheld scanner that can see drugs through drywall like X-ray vision  \n- ❌ No phone app that can detect drugs inside walls  \n- ❌ Standard stud finders cannot detect drugs  \n\n---\n\n## 🔎 What Law Enforcement Uses (High-Level Overview)\n\nThese are specialized tools and usually require legal authority:\n\n### 1️⃣ Drug Detection Dogs\n- Most effective method\n- Can detect odor through walls, vents, and containers\n\n### 2️⃣ Ion Mobility Spectrometry (Trace Detection)\n- Detects microscopic drug particles in air or on surfaces\n- Usually requires access to the space\n\n### 3️⃣ Thermal Imaging\n- Sometimes used if grow operations (like cannabis grows) produce heat\n- Does NOT directly detect drugs — only heat anomalies\n\n### 4️⃣ Ground-Penetrating Radar (GPR)\n- Can detect hidden compartments\n- Cannot identify drugs specifically — only density differences\n\n### 5️⃣ Fiber-Optic Inspection Cameras\n- Requires drilling a small hole\n- Used when there is probable cause\n\n---\n\n## ⚠️ Important Reality\n\nIn residential settings:\n- Hidden drugs behind walls are usually discovered due to:\n  - Smell\n  - Tip-offs\n  - Structural modifications\n  - Utility anomalies\n  - K9 alerts\n\nThere is no legal over-the-counter “drug wall detector.”\n\n---\n\nIf you’re asking because:\n- You suspect something in your property\n- You're a landlord worried about illegal activity\n- You're dealing with a dispute\n\nLet me know the situation (without sharing anything incriminating), and I’ll guide you on **legal and safe next steps** in Canada."
          ]
